  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "To control her blood pressure, Jill’s grandmother takes one half of a pill every other day. If one supply of medicine contains \\(60\\) pills, then the supply of medicine will last approximately",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\) month",
    "B": "\\(4\\) months",
    "C": "\\(6\\) months",
    "D": "\\(8\\) months",
    "E": "\\(1\\) year"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Each whole pill provides two half-pill doses, so \\(60\\) pills provide\n\\[60\\cdot2=120\\text{ doses}.\\]\nOne dose is taken every two days, so these doses cover about \\(120\\cdot2=240\\) days. Using approximately \\(30\\) days per month gives\n\\[240\\div30=8\\text{ months}.\\]\nThe supply lasts approximately \\(8\\) months, choice \\(\\mathrm D\\).",
